    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "McGovern Estates is delighted to present No. 24 Rocky Valley to the market.\r\n\r\nSpanning approximately 313.3 sq.m, No. 24 is an impressive and exceptionally spacious five-bedroom detached family home extending over three storeys. Distinctive in design, this property is flooded with natural light thanks to its expansive multi-aspect glazing, while the rear of the home enjoys stunning views of the Little Sugarloaf mountain.\r\n\r\nThroughout, the home showcases outstanding craftsmanship and elegant finishes, including bespoke cabinetry, plantation shutters, feature Monastic arched doorways, polished Italian porcelain tiles, and other exquisite design details.\r\n\r\nSet on landscaped grounds of c. 1/4 acre that wraps around the property, No. 24 features a private south-facing garden to the rear. \r\n\r\nGenerously proportioned rooms open seamlessly onto a sun-drenched patio and lawn—perfect for modern open-plan living and entertaining—while cosy fireplaces create intimate spaces ideal for relaxing winter evenings.\r\n\r\nPerfectly positioned within the highly sought-after Rocky Valley development, this exceptional home is just a stone’s throw from the N11/M50 road network, providing easy access to local schools and nearby towns and villages including Enniskerry, Bray, Greystones, Delgany, and Roundwood as well as Dublin city, airport and beyond.\r\n\r\nNestled amid tranquil surroundings, the area offers an abundance of amenities, leisure pursuits, and sporting facilities to complement a contemporary lifestyle.\r\n\r\nEach element of this home has been thoughtfully designed to delight the senses and soothe the soul. Viewing of this remarkable property is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hallway\r\nItalian Porcelain tiled flooring, decorative coving, feature radiator covers, gallery stairs to landing, recess lighting.\r\n \r\nLiving Room  \r\nCarpeted flooring, decorative coving, feature  gas fire with ornate porous stone mantle and cast iron inset with polished black Granite hearth, marble, multi-aspect orientation windows, smoke alarm, double doors to south facing garden.\r\n\r\nKitchen Room \r\nTiled flooring, bespoke custom built fully fitted kitchen, floor and wall based storage cupboards, feature island unit with solid wood countertop and sink unit, integrated appliances, extractor hood, 6 ring gas hob/ range style cooker, Porous marble countertop, additional cupboards, wine cooler, recess lighting, over looking rear garden with views of the Sugarloaf.\r\n\r\nDining Room  \r\nTiled flooring, decorative coving, multi-aspect windows.\r\n\r\nStudy Room    \r\nTiled flooring, decorative coving, bespoke office cabinetry, smoke alarm,multi-aspect glazing.\r\n\r\nDownstairs WC  \r\nTiled floor, feature wood panelling, WC, pedestal wash hand basin, radiator cover, feature curved doors.\r\n\r\nUtility Store Room    \r\nPorcelain tiled flooring, decorative coving, recess lighting, smoke alarm, hot press off, extensive gallery landing.\r\n\r\nTV Living Room\r\nSolid Walnut wood flooring, decorative coving, ample glazing, feature gas fire with polished white Granite mantle, hearth and surround, double doors to south facing to Indian Sandstone patio.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\r\nCarpeted flooring, decorative coving, floor to ceiling built in wardrobe, dual aspect windows, walk through wardrobe with ample storage, en-suite off.\r\n\r\nEn Suite\r\nTiled flooring, decorative coving, WC, pedestal wash hand basin, extensive wall mirror, Vogue bath with mains power shower and exquiste Marble surround, extractor fan, external window.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\r\nCarpeted flooring, decorative coving, floor to ceiling built in wardrobe, dual aspect windows overlooking stunning views of the Little Sugarloaf, smoke alarm, en-suite off.\r\n\r\nEn Suite\r\nTiled flooring, decorative coving, WC, pedestal wash hand basin, wall mirror, fully tiled shower unit with mains power shower, extractor fan, external window.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 \r\nCarpeted flooring, floor to ceiling built in wardrobe, overlooking south facing garden, juliette en- suite off.\r\n \r\nEn Suite\r\nTiled flooring, WC, pedestal wash hand basin with tiled splashback, wall mirror, fully tiled shower unit with mains power shower, extractor fan. \r\n\r\nBedroom 4\r\nCarpeted flooring, floor to ceiling built in wardrobe, dual aspect windows overlooking the Sugarloaf, juliette en- suite off.\r\n \r\nEn Suite\r\nTiled flooring, WC, pedestal wash hand basin with tiled splashback, wall mirror, fully tiled shower unit with mains power shower, extractor fan.\r\n\r\nBedroom 5\r\nCarpeted flooring, built in storage, vaulted ceiling, one Velux window, en-suite off.\r\n\r\nEn Suite\r\nTiled flooring, WC, pedestal wash hand basin, bath with part tiled walls, feature mains power shower, wall mirror, recessed storage space.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nOutside Rear\r\nIndian Sandstone patio, cobblelock paving, large grass lawn, mature trees and planting, stunning views of the Little Sugarloaf, exterior lighting and power socket. original stone buit walls, contemporary curved feature wall, 2 x mature fruit bearing vines, mature fruit and specimen trees and shrubs, lawned and gravel grounds.\r\n\r\nOutside Front\r\nCobblelock driveway, off street parking, double garage, mature shrubbery, EV charger, timber framed fencing and side access gates."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Exceptionally spacious 5 bed detached family home \r\nc.1/4 acre site\r\nAn enviable B3 BER \r\nComplimentary use of contemporary & classical design\r\nMulti aspect rooms fill this home with natural light throughout \r\nBespoke kitchen with stunning feature island\r\nFeature Monastic arched doorways\r\nFeature polished italian porcelain tiles\r\nFeature gallery landing with picture window\r\nPlantation shutters in each room\r\nWell proportioned rooms enjoying a mix of grand and intimate spaces\r\nEach bedroom has access to an en suite\r\nPrivate south facing gardens behind mature hedging and specimen trees\r\nStunning views of ‘Little Sugarloaf’ mountain\r\nManicured gardens enjoying both lawn and patio areas.\r\nDetached double garage with potential to convert\r\nGas fired central heating system \r\nHigh speed Broadband available\r\nElectric vehicle charger\r\nOff street parking for mulitple vehicles\r\nBEAM central vacuum system \r\nInternal sound system throughout\r\nVacant possession\r\nEasy access to schools and amenities\r\nExceptionally well located for access to the N11/M50 road networks"
      },
